## Minimal IaC Sketch (Terraform)
```hcl
resource "aws_sfn_state_machine" "sap_incident_response" {
  name     = "sap-incident-response"
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.stepfunctions_role.arn
  definition = file("${path.module}/state_machine.json")
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "cross_account_remediation" {
  name = "sap-remediation-role"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow",
      Principal = { AWS = "arn:aws:iam::123456789:role/sap-incident-response-role" },
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
      Condition = { Bool = { "aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent" = true } }
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_security_group_rule" "sap_isolation" {
  count = 1
  type        = "ingress"
  from_port   = 0
  to_port     = 0
  protocol    = "-1"
  description = "Emergency isolation"
  source_security_group_id = aws_security_group.sap_management.id
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical incident response design using AWS-native tooling in a SAP on AWS context, focusing on automation, speed, and auditable notifications.

## Key Concepts
- CloudWatch alarms and SAP heartbeat monitoring
- EventBridge as automation trigger
- Step Functions orchestration for multi-step recovery
- SSM Run Command for SAP status verification
- VPC security controls for subnet isolation
- SNS for stakeholder notifications

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Lambda skeleton for status check (conceptual)
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ssm = new AWS.SSM();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const params = {
    InstanceIds: ['i-sap-instance'],
    DocumentName: 'AWS-RunShellScript',
    Parameters: {
      commands: ['HDB info | grep -i "overall status"']
    }
  };

  const result = await ssm.sendCommand(params).promise();
  return { status: 'checked', commandId: result.Command.CommandId };
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses advanced multi-account SAP security design involving Nitro Enclaves, ABAC tag mappings, PrivateLink, cross-account KMS control, and DR automation.

## Key Concepts

- Nitro Enclaves for data-in-use isolation
- ABAC mapped to SAP authorizations via AWS tags
- Cross-account KMS key policies and access grants
- PrivateLink for SAP components
- DR failover orchestration and testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Enable Nitro Enclaves on EC2 instance
const { EC2Client, ModifyInstanceAttributeCommand } = require("@aws-sdk/client-ec2");
const ec2 = new EC2Client({region: 'us-east-1'});
await ec2.send(new ModifyInstanceAttributeCommand({
  InstanceId: 'i-0123456789abcdef0',
  EnclaveOptions: { Enabled: true }
}));

// Cross-account KMS policy grant (CDK-like pseudo)
const key = new kms.Key(this, 'SAPDataKey', { enableKeyRotation: true });
key.addToResourcePolicy(new PolicyStatement({
  principals: [new ArnPrincipal('arn:aws:iam::111111111111:root')],
  actions: ['kms:Encrypt','kms:Decrypt','kms:ReEncrypt*','kms:GenerateDataKey*','kms:DescribeKey'],
  resources: ['*']
}));
```

